    "On the other side, a carboxyl group, written C O O H."
   ],
   [
    16.001,
    "Below the carbon, a single hydrogen atom."
   ],
   [
    18.826,
    "And on top, the side chain, called R."
   ],
   [
    21.821,
    "So three named parts: the amino group, the carboxyl group, and R."
   ],
   [
    26.665,
    "The first two follow the same pattern in all of them, with one bent exception, proline, which we meet in lesson two."
   ],
   [
    33.37,
    "R is the part that is characteristic of each amino acid."
   ],
   [
    36.899,
    "It is what makes one amino acid different from another."
